From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: report no selection fade in an external shell session

Purpose: keep a chosen Start menu item off XP's grey log-off screen.
XP behavior: with "Fade out menu items after clicking" (SPI_GETSELECTIONFADE,
on by XP's default UserPreferencesMask) the shell shows the chosen item in
a layered window whose opacity it lowers to 0 over about 350 ms.
Wine before: winex11 sets that opacity as _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY, which
neither the X11 session (no compositing manager) nor win4wine's labwc
shows, so the item stayed opaque until the window went. When the shell
was slow (Firefox starting), the log-off and shutdown dialogs' capture of
the screen was taken before that and kept the item in the grey background.
Change: with the opt-in, SPI_GETSELECTIONFADE reports FALSE, as XP does
with the effect turned off: the item goes with the menu.
Evidence: the nested X11 session no longer maps the fade window (polled
every 10 ms); in the test VM with Firefox starting, the classic menu's
log off and shutdown items left the item on the grey screen before the
change and not after it.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL; the setting itself is kept.
---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index 3d85f0f..d8e988a 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -6693,6 +6693,10 @@ BOOL WINAPI NtUserSystemParametersInfo( UINT action, UINT val, void *ptr, UINT w
         break;
     case SPI_GETSELECTIONFADE:
         ret = get_entry( &entry_SELECTIONFADE, val, ptr );
+        /* win4wine: the X server and win4wine's compositor show no window
+         * opacity, so the shell's fade of a chosen menu item stays opaque
+         * until it ends, and a screen capture can keep it */
+        if (ret && ptr && win4wine_external_shell()) *(BOOL *)ptr = FALSE;
         break;
     case SPI_SETSELECTIONFADE:
         ret = set_entry( &entry_SELECTIONFADE, val, ptr, winini );
